---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = 'July 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy · HyphaeHub" description="How HyphaeHub collects, uses, and protects your data.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-substrate">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/50">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how HyphaeHub LLC ("HyphaeHub", "we", "us") handles
          information when you use our hosted Cloud service and this website. If you run the
          self-hosted Community Edition, your data lives on infrastructure you control and we do
          not receive it, so the collection sections below do not apply to that use.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Information we collect</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li><strong>Account information.</strong> Your name and email address, handled through our identity provider (Auth0) when you sign in.</li>
          <li><strong>Content you enter.</strong> The records you create, such as strains, batches, cultures, jars, harvests, inventory, costs, notes, and any photos you upload.</li>
          <li><strong>Billing information.</strong> If you subscribe to a paid plan, payments are processed by Stripe. We receive limited billing details such as your plan and subscription status. We never see or store full card numbers.</li>
          <li><strong>Organization and activity data.</strong> Your organization membership and role, plus an audit log of actions taken in your organization (who did what, and when).</li>
          <li><strong>Technical data.</strong> Standard log data such as IP address, request time, and browser type, handled by our hosting provider (Cloudflare) to run and secure the service.</li>
          <li><strong>Cookies.</strong> A session cookie to keep you signed in. We do not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">How we use information</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We use your information to provide and maintain the service, sign you in, process
          subscriptions, respond to support requests, keep the service secure, and improve how it
          works. We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use your grow records for
          advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Who we share it with</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We share information only with the service providers we use to run HyphaeHub, and only as
          needed to provide it:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> for hosting, storage, and content delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>Auth0</strong> for authentication and sign-in.</li>
          <li><strong>Stripe</strong> for payment processing on paid plans.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may also disclose information if required by law, to protect our rights or users, or as
          part of a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, in which case we will let you know.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Where your data is stored</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Cloud data is stored on Cloudflare infrastructure and may be processed in the United
          States. We keep your data for as long as your account is active. When you close your
          account or ask us to delete your data, we remove it from our production systems within a
          reasonable period, except where we must keep records to meet a legal obligation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You can access, correct, export, or delete your data at any time from within the app or by
          contacting us. Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights under laws such
          as the Oregon Consumer Privacy Act. To make a request, email
          <a class="font-medium text-hyphae-700 hover:underline" href="mailto:privacy@hyphaehub.io">privacy@hyphaehub.io</a>.
          We will not discriminate against you for exercising these rights.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Security</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We protect data in transit with encryption and limit access to it. No online service can
          promise perfect security, so we cannot guarantee it, but we work to keep your data safe and
          to notify you if something goes wrong.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Children</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          HyphaeHub is not directed to children under 18, and we do not knowingly collect their
          information. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we will remove it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We may update this policy from time to time. When we make material changes, we will update
          the date above and, where appropriate, notify you in the app or by email.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Questions about privacy? Email
          <a class="font-medium text-hyphae-700 hover:underline" href="mailto:privacy@hyphaehub.io">privacy@hyphaehub.io</a>.
          This policy is governed by the laws described in our
          <a class="font-medium text-hyphae-700 hover:underline" href="/terms">Terms and Usage Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
